   "距離": null,
   "简介": {
    "日文": null,
    "英文": "Tokyo Station (Japanese: 東京駅, Hepburn: Tōkyō-eki; pronounced [to̞ːkʲo̞ːe̞kʲi]) is a major railway station and a central rail hub in Chiyoda, Tokyo, Japan. The original station is located in Chiyoda's Marunouchi business district near the Imperial Palace grounds. The newer Eastern extension is not far from the Ginza commercial district. Due to the large area covered by the station, it is divided into the Marunouchi (west) and Yaesu (east) sides in its directional signage.\nThe station opened in 1914 as an integrated terminus for the present-day Tōkaidō Line, Tōhoku Line, and later the Chūō Line,",
    "中文": "東京站（日語：東京駅〔東京驛〕／とうきょうえき〔とうきゃうえき〕，羅馬化：Tōkyō eki），或稱東京車站，位於日本東京都千代田區丸之內一丁目，為東日本旅客鐵道（JR東日本）、東海旅客鐵道（JR東海）、東京地下鐵的鐵路車站。開業於1914年，是日本多條鐵路幹線的端點站、以及新幹線其中4條路線的端點站，為東京主要交通樞紐之一，擁有東京都市中央車站的地位。\n※ 以下需要將JR東日本、JR東海等JR系列公司合稱時，統一以「JR」表記。"
   },
